Lumina SFX — Split License

Choose the terms for the material you use. A game that bundles both the
runtime and sound recipes uses both parts of this license.

1. Code and documentation — MIT

The MIT text below covers engine/, scripts/, adapters/, SKILL.md and the
project's other software, tests and documentation outside the sound library.
The optional measured headphone impulse responses in engine/hrtf/ retain
their Apache License 2.0 terms. Include that directory's LICENSE.txt and
NOTICE.md when distributing the table. The Web Audio native headphone
renderer uses the browser's own data.

