2. Sound library — Lumina Open Game Audio License 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 LuminaBench contributors.

Scope. This part covers the original Lumina sound designs and arrangements
in recipes/, the original library material in sources/, and the selection
and arrangement of catalog.json. It also covers those creative contributions
when embodied in rendered audio or modified versions.

What you can do. You have a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license
to download, copy, render, edit, layer and synchronize these sounds in
personal or commercial games, apps, videos and interactive demos. You may
ship, sell, stream or monetize those projects and their updates, including
the recipes or audio files they need at runtime. Your team and contractors
may share working copies to make and maintain those projects. You may also
fork the repository to contribute improvements. No audio attribution or
credit screen is required. A mention of Lumina SFX is appreciated.

What you cannot do under this license. You may not redistribute, rebrand
or resell the recipe bank or a collection of its rendered sounds as a
competing SFX pack, sample library, training dataset or Agent Skill. This
applies to free and paid offerings, including renamed, modified or
reformatted collections. For example, a game may include hundreds of
working sound assets. Offering those assets as a downloadable sound pack
for other developers requires separate permission from the rights holders.

Source recordings. Third-party recordings retain their original terms,
identified in sources/recordings.json. CC0 and public-domain material
remains independently available under those terms. This license grants
only rights held by the Lumina contributors. Earlier releases remain
available under the terms under which they were distributed.

The sound library is provided as is, without warranty. To the extent
permitted by law, the contributors are not liable for damages arising
from its use.
